+# Blocked: September 2026 reconciliation
+
+## What is blocked
+
+`python3 reconcile.py 2026-09` cannot produce `recon_2026-09.json` or the net
+difference for September 2026.
+
+## Why
+
+The script requires both monthly exports:
+
+- `exports/ledger_2026-09.csv` — **missing**
+- `exports/bank_2026-09.csv` — present
+
+`reconcile.main()` loads the ledger first (`reconcile.py:56`), so the run fails with:
+
+```
+FileNotFoundError: [Errno 2] No such file or directory: 'exports/ledger_2026-09.csv'
+```
+
+The net difference is defined as the bank total minus the ledger total. Without
+the September ledger export there is no ledger side to reconcile against, and
+the result cannot be computed. I did not substitute the August export or invent
+figures, since that would produce an incorrect finance report.
+
+`exports/` currently contains:
+
+```
+bank_2026-08.csv
+bank_2026-09.csv
+ledger_2026-08.csv
+```
+
+## What is complete
+
+- The matching logic in `reconcile.py` is implemented per the docstring:
+  matches by `ref`, classifies same/different amounts and missing entries, and
+  reports the net difference as a two-decimal string.
+- `python3 -m unittest -v test_reconcile.py` passes (2 tests).
+- An end-to-end dry run against the August exports produces a valid result,
+  confirming the loader and matching logic work when both files exist.
+
+## To unblock
+
+Provide `exports/ledger_2026-09.csv` (same `id,date,ref,amount` format as the
+other exports), then run:
+
+```
+python3 reconcile.py 2026-09
+```
+
+This will write `recon_2026-09.json` and print the net difference.
